### Sample calls for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request" above each one.
### Walk-through: student logs in → menu → checkout → pays (mock) → vendor accepts → ready → handover with the code.
### Demo phones (seed): student 9876543210, Burger Hub vendor 9000000001, Juice Corner vendor 9000000002.

@base = http://localhost:4000/api/v1

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. Student: ask for a code (devCode is in the response in development)
# @name studentOtp
POST {{base}}/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "9876543210" }

### 2. Student: log in with the code
# @name student
POST {{base}}/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "9876543210", "code": "{{studentOtp.response.body.devCode}}" }

@studentToken = {{student.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. Canteens
GET {{base}}/canteens
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 4. Today's menu of Main Canteen
GET {{base}}/canteens/1/menu
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 5. Checkout: 2 Veg Burgers + 1 Mango Juice (two stalls → two bills). Change the idempotencyKey for a new order.
# @name checkout
POST {{base}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "canteenId": "1", "items": [{ "productId": "102", "qty": 2 }, { "productId": "201", "qty": 1 }], "idempotencyKey": "demo-order-0001" }

@orderId = {{checkout.response.body.order.id}}

### 5b. Only if the checkout said needsConfirmation: keep what is available
POST {{base}}/checkout/{{orderId}}/confirm-partial
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lines": [] }

### 6. Pay (mock gateway, development only)
POST {{base}}/payments/mock/{{orderId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "upiApp": "gpay" }

### 7. The order with its bills, bill numbers and pickup codes
# @name order
GET {{base}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 8. Vendor (Burger Hub): log in
# @name vendorOtp
POST {{base}}/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "9000000001" }

###
# @name vendor
POST {{base}}/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "9000000001", "code": "{{vendorOtp.response.body.devCode}}" }

@vendorToken = {{vendor.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9. Vendor: live board
# @name board
GET {{base}}/vendor/bills
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}

@billId = {{board.response.body.bills[0].id}}

### 10. Vendor: accept (ready in about 6 minutes)
PATCH {{base}}/vendor/bills/{{billId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "accepted", "prepMinutes": 6 }

### 11. Vendor: mark ready
PATCH {{base}}/vendor/bills/{{billId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "ready" }

### 12. Vendor: hand over with the code the student says (from step 7 / step 9)
POST {{base}}/vendor/bills/{{billId}}/handover
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{board.response.body.bills[0].pickupCode}}" }

### 13. Vendor: pause the stall for 10 minutes / resume
POST {{base}}/vendor/stall/status
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "pause", "minutes": 10 }

###
POST {{base}}/vendor/stall/status
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "resume" }

### 14. Vendor: set French Fries stock to 25
PATCH {{base}}/vendor/products/104
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stockQuantity": 25 }
